Many of my games have a particular annoying pattern to them and I wonder 
if others have had the same experience...and found ways of overcoming it 
perhaps.

If I get a somewhat viable character going who advances to about level 
10 experience, that's the best the character is ever going to get.  At 
10, or maybe 11, the character has (for example) good armor, a nice 
weapon or two, some useful magical items....  From that point on, traps, 
rust monsters, succubus in whatever plurals, and various other monsters 
and misadventures tend to drain items, levels, enchantments, abilities, 
and what-have-you.

In my top-twenty scores, there are a few results of stupid decisions, a 
few "soldier with wand of death" types, and a whole lot of characters 
who just wore down to a point where they became fodder for things they 
could have dealt with easily some time before.  Or games where I've 
simply quit, realizing that it's not much fun playing a hopeless 
loser...I get enough of that in real life.  :-)

I don't have a specific question, but the closest concerns traps, I 
suppose.  Not only do I tend to lose potions, scrolls and armor 
effectiveness to fire and water, but I also seem to lose 2 pets per game 
to those, and falling rocks and pits and rolling boulders.  Do people 
typically spend time searching before taking each step?  (Even my 
rangers don't find enough of the traps in advance.)


